{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Behold, the nations are like a drop from a bucket.</b> Like a drop that falls from the bucket, and it is of no consequence to it:" "<b>And like dust.</b> It is the fine dust from which you cut and crush fine dust (Exodus 30:36), and since all human beings are nothing compared to Him, with whom does He take counsel:" "<b>Shall take.</b> Shall cast, like ויטילו את הכלים [and they cast the vessels] (Jonah 1:5), but it is from a different root, and Rabbi Jonah the grammarian said that יטול is from the nif'al paradigm, by a distant route, or the meaning of יטול is 'shall lift,' like נוטל:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:08.543242862Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}